The @char was a neutral male human Monk
The strategy was to find a =oSlowDigestion (mostly exploring sokoban
and kicking sinks) as soon as possible and cure hunger with prayer.

I had a great starting level, with a sink (great for identifying =oSD)
on the starting room and 2 co-aligned altars.

On dlvl 6 (oracle) I found a great bones from EricHerman. The 2
greatest assets were =SD and [MagicResistance, but there were also
lots of goodies: a Blessed +4 helm of brilliance, a ?Scare Monster
(turned to dust, but allowed me to identify it; however I did not find
another ?SM in the entire game), some potions, a magic whistle, some
wands (the most important was Cancellation, with still a few charges
left), stethoscope, blindfold, oil lamp, a key and a bag of tricks. It
also had some other nice rings, but I lost them on the sink trying to
id the =oSD (the greatest loss was protection from shape changers,
which was the only ring on the entire dungeon).

I was now pretty much set up, and proceded to do sokoban. It had not
only the "oReflection, but also a can of grease, plus the usual gold.
I established there my stash and went to do the mines. The minetown
was another bones (Numlock) file, but the stores were mostly
untouched, and the altar was co-aligned (+4 AC protection of 1st
donation).
General shop had a $500 wand (which I only Id'd as death when I got
the castle wand), another bag of tricks and another can of grease. I
also used it to do some price id on rings and potions.
After all that and some stashing, I went to get Numlock's possessions.
It was another wizard, and appart from a magic lamp and some potions
there was nothing important.  While searching the rest of the mines I
found 2 touchstones (which later came in handy to guarantee maxed
luck) and a bag of holding. The mines end was the mimics version, and
appart from the luckstone and gems it had a tooled horn (usefull for
air elementals). From the mines loot I also got a +2 dwarvish
roundshield and a +1 pair of iron shoes.

On dlvl 8, yet another bones (DerekStyl), this time a samurai with
nothing much appart from speed boots, which in any case I would only
Id much later, on the Valley of Death. And I did find some more speed
boots around. On this level I also found a crystal ball, but I don't
think it was bones related.

On dlvl 20 I found a poly trap, which I used to get good pets. The
first was "Mini me", a minotaur. On dlvl 23 I found some water walking
boots, after I had crossed medusa level with =oLev. Right above the
castle, I was flayed, but didn't lose too much information. Mini me
took care of the mindflayer (as well as some other nasties, like some
L and the occasional golden naga).  The castle entrance had the
occasional L summon, but with levitation, conflict and Mini me,
eventually it was all cleared out.
Around turn 42K I had my stash established on the Valley, like I
usually do, and started exploring Gehennom. I still did not have the
eyes, but even if I had I would not have used them because they
promote stupid errors that break weaponless on digging.
By this time I was having some care with my pet, which implied
disabling poly traps and level teleport traps. It also implied killing
quicky t and purple worms, and tinning shape changers corpses. Even
so, at dlvl 29 a (master??) mind flayer killed Mini me (and itself,
since I had reflection) with a /oD.

Back at dlvl 20, I got a baby purple worm (called Bubu) from the poly
trap. After training it unto a purple worm, I continued Gehennom
exploration. Juiblex's swamp was yet another bones(SonjaElen), with
Juiblex already killed. Since SonjaElen's possessions were under
water, and I never did bother to identify "oMagical Breathing, I never
knew what the bones held. One of these days I'll take a look at that
ttyrec/dumplog.

After exploring until level 34, and having found all first 3 demon
lairs I decided it was alchemy time. I diluted all non important
potions to bless them, and alchemised 22 potions of full healing. I
kept some and quaffed the rest to get to 231 HP. Then I went to Master
Kaen with my level 26 purple worm. Since my starting move was
cancelling him, and I had some full healing potions handy, all I had
to do was to wait for the ever heart-warming message: 'Bubu bites
Master Kaen.  Bubu swallows Master Kaen.  "Burrrrp!'.

Back at Gehennom exploration, a moment of distraction was all it took
to Bubu to eat a shape changer and turn into a Barrow wight. Since I
was really buffed up I decided to continue petless for a while, but on
the very next level (Orcus town) a Olog-hai reading a cursed ?CM
created a horde of monsters (with master mind flayer included). On the
confusion I lost quite a lot of hit points and ended up falling a hole
from a fleeing monster's wand of dig. I did find Vlad's tower (always
a nice place to pray for nutrition), but the top level was blocked
with a master mind flayer. Having had enough with all the mother-f****
snakes (nasties) on the mother-f**** plane (dungeon), I decided to go
get another pet. I evaded Orcus with a C!GL, and carried up Bubu to
dlvl 20 again. This time I settled for a storm giant, which was
promptly killed by yet another master mind flayer on Baalzebub's lair.
Luckily, I had a couple of non-identified directional wands, and it
turned out one was turn undead. I had already identified the wand of
polymorph, so I didn't have to worry about screwing up a very advanced
10 conduct game that way like I did a couple of weeks ago (and yes, it
was another master mind flayer with wand of death...).
Back to orcus town, and since I entered from the upstairs with Orcus
already awake, it was easy killing him/it before he/it emptied the
/oD.

A few levels below, an unexpected poly trap on the way of Bubu (whom I
had called to take care of another h) ruined my pet again. Back on
dlvl 20 (I didn't want to play around in Gehennom), Bubu turned into a
Jabberwock, which would be its last form until it died. Also, since
during its previous form Bubu had put on a "oR, it was now immune to
ray attacks. Since I had established final stash on Vlad tower, I took
this opportunity to go buy candles (I always buy candles near the end
of the game in case some b eats my stash, as it has happened in the
past).

Eventually I marked the vibrating square on level 45, I cleared
Rodney's tower and made my final preparations. Among those
preparations was leaving a small stash on dlvl 1: lots of blessed
potions of fruit juice for nutrition (I don't think I drank any), /oCM
near the altar In case I needed to take care of prayer timeout (didn't
use), lots and lots of /oDig for plane of earth (the portal was kind
of near), some !oParalysis and holy water and extra armor in case I
got something burnt/rotted (didn't need).
I also drank !oGL for intrinsic teleport control, since I had
=oTeleportation and it was usefull getting out of Gehennom. Finally, I
let myself get weak from hunger and prayed to start the ascention run
with maxed nutrition.

The ascention run:
I went to wake Rodney with AC -15 and 257 HP and a tame level 23
Jabberwock on turn ~84K. I had 3 /oD, 2 of them partly used, and I
missed a few shots. I also had to make sure I didn't hit Bubu with a
death ray, since it had died some time before, and therefore lost its
"oRef. In any case, eventually I did hit Rodney, grabbed the book of
dead and rushed to the perform the invocation ritual. Since Bubu ate a
purple-worm corpse and would stay immobile for quite some time I
decided to leave it there and pick it up on the way up.
I did Moloch's sanctum level without conflict to spare nutrition (I
had =FA and =SD), and it was a bit more though than I expected. Even
so, I got (just) a bit of help from a black dragon. My life
occasionaly went to red, but I had enough B!oFH to spend.
I located the entrance with a /Secret Door Detection, /oDeathed (by
this time one wand was empty) the high priest, got the REAL amulet of
Yendor and C!GL out of there. The mysterious force was annoying, but I
must admit it could have been much worse, and I did pick up Bubu on
the way up. Rodney appeared 2 times (/oDeathed) and I even got an
Archon on dlvl 16 (/oTeleport).

The planes:
On the plane of earth, I decided to spare my /oD, and hit Rodney with
!oParalysis. Even so he managed to steal the amulet, but no-teleport
works for both ways and I got it back the hard way. Since I didn't
know how many charges I had on the crystal ball, I decided to keep it
to the plane of fire, and just went checking every cavern wielding "oY
for warmth tips.
For air, I used =oFA and =Lev. I started to race to the right side of
the level, and played the horn when engulfed by E. Somewhere halfway,
Bubu died. On the right side I started zapping /oSDD until I found the
portal. Since the E did not let me progress, I traded FA for conflict,
and it was much better. Near the portal I removed =C and put on =SD
again.
On fire I used my one and only charge of the crystal ball.
On water I decided to avoid stupid deaths and wore oilskin cloak and
levitation boots. Since I had no more charges on the ball, I started
zapping /SDD, but I accidentally entered it since it was hidden under
a scroll.

On astral I put on my boots of jumping (but it would take some time
before I got unburdened), my =FA (so I could hit some nasties with
!Paralysis) and sometimes also my =C.
Since I had enough nutrition resources, I went to Famine's altar
first. Facing Famine I also learned I had only 1 non-empty /oD. I had
lots of /oTeleport, so I used them often on the blocking monsters.
Eventually I found that was the lawful altar, so I went back.

Right before entering the central section (Death's) I finally
remembered to quaff my B!oS and got unburdened, so now I could jump. I
paralysed Death with a potion and raced to the altar, which was the
correct one.

Next time I want to do a similar game, but strict vegan + atheist
instead of foodless.

